          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Values arrive one field at a time rather than one record at a time, so a\ncolumn is written once and read down instead of across. A flow sequence may\nwrap onto the next line, and a block sequence says the same thing in the\nform a hand-editing author usually reaches for."
        }
      ],
      "position": [
